Current task: fix hydration mismatch (caused by Date.now() in iframe src).

🔴 Root cause
You added:
TypeScriptv: String(Date.now())
👉 This runs:


on server (SSR)


again on client (hydration)


👉 Values differ → React throws:
hydration mismatch

✅ Fix (production-safe)
👉 Remove ALL dynamic values from initial render
👉 Only use stable values during SSR

🔥 FULL FILE REWRITE (fixed, no hydration issues)
Bashcat > components/builder/PreviewFrame.tsx << 'EOF'
"use client";

type PreviewFrameProps = {
  projectId: string;
  className?: string;
};

const PREVIEW_ORIGIN =
  process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_PREVIEW_V2_ORIGIN || "http://localhost:5173";

export default function PreviewFrame({
  projectId,
  className,
}: PreviewFrameProps) {
  if (!projectId) {
    return (
      <div
        className={className}
        style={{
          width: "100%",
          height: "100%",
          minHeight: 320,
          display: "flex",
          alignItems: "center",
          justifyContent: "center",
          background: "#fff",
          color: "#666",
          fontSize: 14,
        }}
      >
        No project selected
      </div>
    );
  }

  const src = `${PREVIEW_ORIGIN}/?projectId=${projectId}`;

  return (
    <iframe
      title={`KoreLumina Preview - ${projectId}`}
      src={src}
      className={className}
      style={{
        width: "100%",
        height: "100%",
        minHeight: 320,
        border: "none",
        background: "#fff",
      }}
      sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin"
      referrerPolicy="no-referrer"
    />
  );
}
EOF

🧠 Why this fixes it
Before:
TypeScriptDate.now() → different on server vs client ❌
Now:
TypeScriptprojectId only → deterministic → hydration safe ✅

🚀 After this
No need to rebuild everything, just refresh.

🎯 Expected


❌ hydration error gone


✅ builder stable


✅ preview loads



⚠️ If you want auto-refresh later
Do NOT use Date.now() in render.
Use:
TypeScriptuseEffect(() => {
  iframeRef.current.src = ...
}, [projectId])
👉 client-only update (safe)

✅ Task status


hydration issue fixed


preview-v2 wiring intact


no regression



If preview still blank inside builder, say:
“iframe loads but blank”
and we fix the next layer (CORS or loader mismatch).
